  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output 3.1. Increased capacity of Member States to formulate and implement national employment policies in response to the COVID-19 crisis</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Led by the Department of Labour and Industrial Relations (DLIR) and in consultation with various government agencies and social partners, the Papua New Guinea National Employment Policy (PNG NEP) was developed and launched in 2022. The country&#x2019;s first ever national employment policy is anchored in the ILO Employment Policy Convention, 1964 (No. 122) and makes specific reference to the COVID-19 crisis and recovery. The PNG NEP promotes and fosters equal participation and inclusion of men, women, youth and people with special needs in socio-economic development, decision-making and service delivery process at all levels. The overarching PNG NEP will enhance the PNG National Youth Policy (2020&#x2013;2030) and other related youth policies to promote decent employment opportunities for young people in PNG. The ILO provided technical assistance on the NEP through a series of advisory engagements with DLIR, including technical reviews and comments on the draft NEP and the development of a work plan.</narrative>
   </description>
